      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BETTOR WASH UP (6) settled close to the pace and kept finding to finish third last start over 1609m at Bunbury, adding to his sound recent efforts. Big chance in a similar assignment. GAMETIME (8) good effort to finish third two starts ago at Bunbury but was less impressive at his latest appearance over 2100m at Bunbury, beaten 19 metres into sixth after being up on the pace. Gets a soft run on the inside of the second line but may need luck at some point. Certainly cannot be faulted after that last effort. Good enough to put himself back in the winners' stall. CAPTURE THE MOMENT (1) didn't do a bad job when sixth over 1730m at Central Wheatbelt last time out. Each-way chance. HIGHLY FLAMMABLE (7) is the next elect off a last-start win by 5.5 metres at Central Wheatbelt over 1730m.",
